   "Essential expenditure growth is modeled to moderate to +2.6% in 2027 from +6.7% in 2026, primarily due to lower energy cost pressures.",
   "The firm has revised its 2026 forecasts downward, now expecting 2026 DPI growth of +4.0% (vs. +4.7% previously) and pre-savings DCF growth of +3.0% (vs. +3.7% previously).",
   "Household balance sheets remain strong with the net worth-to-disposable personal income ratio near all-time highs, though consumer sentiment remains low.",
   "The savings rate is expected to rise to 3.6% in 2027 from 3.4% in 2026, which leads to a lower savings-adjusted DCF forecast of +3.9% for 2027."
